+# PJM M-3 gas-CC commitment bridge — evidence + mechanism (2026-07)
+
+**Lane:** PJM frontier readiness. **Mechanism:** `pjm_gas_commitment_bridge`
+(default off, PJM-gated). **Status:** implemented + unit-tested; probe solve
+pending. This is the on-record "admissible mechanism tried" that a PJM frontier
+declaration needs (`docs/calibration-and-validation-methodology.md` §5;
+`DIAGNOSIS-pjm-2025-phase-drift-and-zonal-structure-2026-07.md` §6, M-3).
+
+## 1. What it is
+
+The PJM analogue of `ercot_gas_commitment_bridge` (ERCOT-63) and the CAISO RA
+must-offer bridge — the **same ISO-neutral P1-native detector**
+(`model.commitment.caiso_ra_mustoffer_min_gen`: min-down physics + the
+startup-restart inequality on the model's OWN base-cost **P0** run pattern and
+duals) routed onto the PJM merchant gas-CC fleet. A CC the P0 pattern runs
+before AND after an idle gap is held at `min_load_frac × pmax × availability`
+across the gap when either (a) the gap is shorter than its physical min-down (a
+restart bar), or (b) re-paying its published startup cost exceeds the net cost
+of holding at min-load priced at the model's own P0 duals (the standard UC
+restart inequality). Bounded to one DA operating day
+(`DA_COMMITMENT_HORIZON_HOURS`) on the economic leg.
+
+**Target residual:** PJM's model-side ~1 h-early lead (§1c) and the D-1p
+flat-overnight residual (§4) — one phenomenon: P1 has no overnight commitment
+posture, so it cycles CC off between run-days and restarts at the exact
+economic crossing while reality carries commitment inertia (measured overnight
++$2–6 LMP overshoot).
+
+**Forward-native / admissibility (rules 13/18):** no measured generation
+enters the solve — only the model's own P0 run pattern + physical constants +
+one measured scalar (`min_load_frac`). Regenerates in any forecast year.
+
+## 2. Committed-state evidence + the min_load_frac scalar
+
+`scripts/derive_pjm_gas_bridge_params.py` — frozen against residuals (rule 23;
+re-derive only when the offers corpus updates). Source: PJM DataMiner2
+`energy_market_offers` feed (`data/raw/pjm-energy-offers/`, gitignored — the
+non-member redistribution restriction + ~1–2 GB size; regenerate with
+`scripts/fetch_pjm_energy_offers.py`). Cross-season 2024 (Jan/Apr/Jul/Oct):
+
+| quantity | value |
+|---|---|
+| **min_load_frac** (cap-weighted p50 `avg_ecomin/avg_ecomax`, CC segment) | **0.564** |
+| CC-like units / total EcoMax | 302 / 76.8 GW |
+| `avg_ecomin/avg_ecomax` quartiles (unweighted) | 0.52 / 0.63 / 0.77 |
+| CC unit-hours with `avg_ecomin>0`, overnight h0–6 | **0.968** |
+| CC unit-hours with `avg_ecomin>0`, midday h12–18 | 0.968 |
+
+**CC identification** is by unit PHYSICS (the offers carry no fuel label; the
+`unit_code` is hashed), using the SAME frozen segmentation as
+`scripts/derive_pjm_offer_surface.py` (G-22 §2): per-unit median `min_runtime`
+∈ (2, 16] h AND median `ecomin/ecomax` > 0.2, excluding nuclear-like baseload
+(median ratio ≥ 0.95 AND EcoMax ≥ 800 MW) and zero-offer hydro/PS/storage
+(median top-of-curve < $1). The 76.8 GW total matches PJM's gas-CC fleet
+(sanity check). 0.564 sits physically alongside the ERCOT committed-CC p50
+(0.574, 60-Day DAM disclosure) — both merchant gas-CC.
+
+**The overnight evidence** (0.968 at h0–6, equal to midday) is the market-side
+confirmation that committed PJM CC units carry an LSL floor through the
+overnight hours rather than cycling cold — the counterpart of the model's
+flat-overnight dispatch residual the bridge targets.
+
+## 3. Attribution / gates
+
+- **D-2 id:** `MECH_PJM_GAS_COMMITMENT_BRIDGE = 18` — its own id (distinct from
+  the ERCOT bridge's 17) so per-ISO attribution/ablation stay independent (the
+  `MECH_ST_GAS_MUSTRUN_PER_PLANT` precedent). Merchant floor → subject to the
+  D-2/C8 forced-share gate; carries a D-3 ablation entry
+  (`{"pjm_gas_commitment_bridge": False}`).
+- **D-4 window:** `(MECH_PJM_GAS_COMMITMENT_BRIDGE, "CC_REGULAR") = (0, 24)` —
+  economic self-windowing (idle gaps between run-days); off-window binding is 0
+  by construction (rule 12: window + driver + forward story all stated).
+- **Rule 19:** mutually exclusive with the PJM path-B reserve fleet mask
+  (`pjm_reserve_commitment_scoped`) — both replace the P1 fleet; enforced loud
+  at `build_pjm_gas_bridge_p1_prep`. The keeper uses `pjm_reserve_pergen`
+  (kwargs hook only), so no conflict.
+
+## 4. Wiring
+
+- `config/scenarios.py`: `pjm_gas_commitment_bridge` (off),
+  `pjm_gas_bridge_min_load_frac=0.564`, `pjm_gas_bridge_startup` (on),
+  `pjm_gas_bridge_da_horizon` (on) + `TIER_TAGS`.
+- `pipeline/commitment.py`: `_pjm_gas_bridge_floor` + `build_pjm_gas_bridge_p1_prep`.
+- `runner.py` + `scripts/run_calibration.py`: built at the P0→P1 seam, added to
+  the `p1_fleet_prep` `or` chain (ISO-exclusive; forecast + backcast parity).
+- `data/floor_mechanisms.py`, `scripts/legitimacy_diagnostics.py`: id + name +
+  ablation + D-4 window.
+- Tests: `tests/test_pjm_gas_commitment_bridge.py` (8 cases: gate/ISO guards,
+  overnight floor + tag, startup/DA-horizon legs, CT-never-floored, rule-19
+  raise, registry).
+
+## 5. Probe plan (pending solve)
+
+Baseline = **pjm-115** (the current keeper `pjmcong1_east_cut` recipe +
+`gas_daily_shape` interp-fix). A/B via `replay_keeper.py`:
+
+```
+# Arm A (pjm-115 base):  replay keeper --set gas_daily_shape=true
+# Arm B (M-3 probe):     replay keeper --set gas_daily_shape=true --set pjm_gas_commitment_bridge=true
+```
+
+Full span 2023–2025 in one bundle (rule 16). Adjudicate on: overnight LMP
+overshoot / D-1p flat-overnight residual (structure, not MAE — rule 1), the
+C8 forced-share (< 30 % of CC energy at the floor) and D-4 off-window (< 5 %)
+gates, and no cross-criterion regression. Register the result (keeper or
+rejected probe) on the dashboard the same session (rule 15).
